## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical, DR-aware design for beginner-level Azure data pipelines, focusing on cross-region configuration, parameterization, and basic upsert strategies.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Data Factory pipelines and parameterization
- ADLS Gen2 storage and region-redundant options
- Mapping Data Flows with schema drift handling
- Azure Synapse Analytics star schema loading
- Idempotent upserts via MERGE
- Simple DR strategy and runbook steps

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example snippet: parameter schema
{
  "name": "IngestPipeline",
  "properties": {
    "parameters": {
      "Region": { "type": "string" },
      "Date": { "type": "string" }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test failover without affecting production?
- What monitoring and alerting would you add to verify data freshness after failover?

Why This Is Asked
- Tests end-to-end Azure data engineering: ingestion, governance, lineage, schema drift, and disaster recovery.

Key Concepts
- Delta Lake on ADLS Gen2, Delta Live Tables, Azure Schema Registry, Purview, Event Hubs, SFTP ingestion, cross-region DR, backfill with time travel, data quality gates.

Code Example
```javascript
// High-level pseudo-setup for DLT-like pipeline (language tag as required)
const domainContract = fetchSchemaFromRegistry('telemetry');
const stream = readFromEventHub('telemetry');
const batch = readFromSFTP('/daily/transactions.csv');
const enriched = stream.union(batch).transform(/* drift-tolerant logic */);
writeDeltaLake(enriched, '/lake/telemetry');
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement cross-domain schema evolution without breaking downstream consumers?
- How would you validate lineage completeness across streaming and batch paths in Purview?

## Why This Is Asked
This asks for practical rollback capability in a beginner pipeline, ensuring data integrity and lineage even when schema drift occurs.

## Key Concepts
- Data Factory pipelines
- Parquet point-in-time backups
- Rollback strategies and idempotence
- Purview lineage integration

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-rollback snippet
if (!validationPassed) {
  // restore target from backup
  copy("/backup/pt-20260310", "/synapse/target");
  // record rollback
  tagRun(runId, "rollback");
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate backup cleanup and retention?
- How would you test rollback in a dev environment?
